    {
      "id": "14689668",
      "title": "Validating Forms & Inputs",
      "lectureOrder": 89,
      "videoOrder": 79,
      "sourceHash": "c83a0ac45b5b762f6c38ca1b8f2fadfbb5843cf209a6b971df7bfd285f6431e4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.48,
          "end": 5,
          "en": "Now, regarding the bindings, this is it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.03,
          "end": 10.94,
          "en": "Now I want to dive into validation because that is another important task when you're working with form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.94,
          "end": 13.91,
          "en": "inputs and with user input in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.15,
          "end": 21.83,
          "en": "And the question is which capabilities does Svelte have when it comes to offering help on validating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.83,
          "end": 22.38,
          "en": "input?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.4,
          "end": 29.6,
          "en": "And the answer is non svelte is not a complete framework that would give you a complete built in validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 29.6,
          "end": 30.4,
          "en": "solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.41,
          "end": 36.11,
          "en": "Instead, it gives you the tools to build your own one, or you use certain packages that help you with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 36.11,
          "end": 40.54,
          "en": "validation and JavaScript and you then incorporate them into your svelte app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 40.55,
          "end": 45.38,
          "en": "Now for this course here I'll build my own very simple validation logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 45.38,
          "end": 50,
          "en": "But in general you should be aware that there is no built in help.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 50,
          "end": 52.85,
          "en": "So for example, if we have a input down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 53.68,
          "end": 55.81,
          "en": "And that should be an email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 55.81,
          "end": 62.11,
          "en": "Then of course, setting this to type email gives us some automatic support from the browser if we now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 62.11,
          "end": 64,
          "en": "put this into a form here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.43,
          "end": 68.32,
          "en": "Then we also add a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 69.2,
          "end": 72.47,
          "en": "Which has a type of submit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "Then here on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.45,
          "end": 78.67,
          "en": "Submit, we can actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "Prevent the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "And with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 90.34,
          "end": 97.21000000000001,
          "en": "And with that, if I then also give the button some text like save if I do try to submit this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "With the wrong value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 108.81,
          "en": "You see, I get this automatic help by the browser, but you might not want to rely on this, or you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "might want your own validation logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 115.07,
          "en": "And in such a case you, as I just said, have to build it on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "So for example, here you could bind the value to entered email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 123.75,
          "en": "Which should be a variable, of course, that you have to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 125.41,
          "end": 131.68,
          "en": "And then if you want to confirm whether that is valid or not and whether the entire form is valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 131.71,
          "end": 133.15,
          "en": "you could have a.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 135.46,
          "end": 143.41,
          "en": "Reactive expression here where we have form is valid and that simply now contains some logic which checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 143.41,
          "end": 147.46,
          "en": "everything that needs to be checked to control whether it is valid or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 147.49,
          "end": 152.89,
          "en": "We can also say form is valid, is false initially, and then we add a if check here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 156.07999999999998,
          "end": 163.52,
          "en": "If and then you have all your conditions like entered email includes an Add sign, which is of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 163.52,
          "end": 165.35,
          "en": "a very trivial check for email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 165.35,
          "end": 169.88,
          "en": "You could definitely have a more advanced one and you set form is valid to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 169.88,
          "end": 172.7,
          "en": "If that is the case or you set it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 172.7,
          "end": 174.26,
          "en": "If that is not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 174.26,
          "end": 178.64,
          "en": "And this is what I mean, you build your own validation solution because there is no built in one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 178.64,
          "end": 180.26,
          "en": "So here is my own logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 180.29,
          "end": 186.26,
          "en": "My entered email is valid if it includes an Add sign and I said form is valid based on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 187.42,
          "end": 192.46,
          "en": "And then down there I can, for example, disable the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 193.17,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "By checking if form is valid and if it is not valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 197.19,
          "end": 198.47,
          "en": "Hence the exclamation mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 199.97,
          "en": "This is set to disabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 204.18,
          "en": "So now with that we actually get an error because.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 204.85,
          "end": 209.47,
          "en": "Entered email initially is undefined and we can't call includes on undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 209.5,
          "end": 211.15,
          "en": "We can only call it on a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 211.15,
          "end": 213.67000000000002,
          "en": "So we should initialize this with an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 213.67000000000002,
          "end": 219.57999999999998,
          "en": "But now with that variable initialization change, you see the button is disabled and it stays disabled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 219.57999999999998,
          "end": 220.99,
          "en": "until there is an at sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 221.02,
          "end": 226.21,
          "en": "Of course, this technically still isn't a valid email address, but you could implement a more elaborate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 226.21,
          "end": 230.01,
          "en": "validation check with regular expressions and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 230.02,
          "end": 232.15,
          "en": "So now this works, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "And removed prevent default again or my removed it for me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 237.32999999999998,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "So this is how you can implement validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 244.11,
          "en": "Of course, this doesn't stop you from providing a nice user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 244.11,
          "end": 247.53,
          "en": "It just means that you have to write a little bit more logic for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 249.79,
          "end": 255.1,
          "en": "You can, for example, also add your own styles to the input if it is not valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 255.13,
          "end": 260.44,
          "en": "For example, here we could add a class and we could check if entered email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 261.09,
          "end": 263.43,
          "en": "Includes an Add sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 263.43,
          "end": 268.86,
          "en": "And of course, you could also put that check into a function so that you only call a function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 268.86,
          "end": 269.91,
          "en": "and.",
          "zh": ""
        },
